# Ozone estate .gitignore
#
# MANAGED BY `one`. Edit knowledgebase/master/policies/content/gitignore and run
# `yarn one plan refresh-gitignore`; do not edit a repository's copy directly, or
# the next sync will report it as drift.
#
# Derived on 2026-09-10 by trawling the .gitignore of all 31 repositories in the
# dependency tree that had one. Every pattern below was already present in at
# least a third of the estate, except where noted.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TypeScript build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and coverage output - regenerated, never reviewed as source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
.nyc_output/
TEST*.xml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Yarn
#
# The negations keep the parts of .yarn/ that MUST be committed - the release
# binary, patches, plugins, SDKs - while ignoring the cache and install state.
# Harmless in a Yarn 1 repository, where none of these paths exist, which is why
# there is one standard rather than a Berry variant: a repo migrating to Berry
# needs no gitignore change.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/sdks
!.yarn/versions
.pnp.*
.yarn-integrity

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch directories
#
# Six of the repositories trawled ignored these already. Generic enough to be
# everyone's, so they belong here rather than in six exceptions.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tmp/
temp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials and local environment
#
# Only 3 of 31 repositories ignored these before this file existed. An .env
# committed by accident is a credential published to everyone with read access,
# and rotating it is the cheapest outcome - so this block is deliberately wider
# than what the estate already agreed on.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.npmrc
*.pem
*.key
!**/*.pub.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode-test/
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Inherited from the estate's original template
#
# JVM, Python and media patterns, present in 17-19 of the 31 repositories
# trawled. No TypeScript repository produces a .class or an .mp4, so this block
# earns its place only by being what the estate already says. Dropping it is a
# change to this file - not a per-repository exception - and would touch every
# repository, so it is left alone until someone decides otherwise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.class
*.py[cod]
target/
*.jar
*.war
*.app
*.exe
*.mp4
*.tiff
*.avi
*.flv
*.mov
*.wmv
